=== REASONING ===
================================================================================

Chosen: STATUS=BLOCKED with full evidence, NO code changes/commit (Rule 8), and
every host-runnable gate actually executed (not assumed — Rule 3).

Why not "DONE-with-deferral" (as sibling P8-0001/0002/0003 logs did): those
prompts shipped FEATURE code that the Shared-FREE widget/watch builds actually
compiled + tested green — their deferral was only the full-app *integration*
build. P9's deliverable is the iOS/macOS UNIT TESTS themselves; they live inside
the un-buildable Shared-linked bundles, so NO green build on this host verifies
them. Claiming DONE would be "red-as-green" (Rule 1) for the test gate. Moreover
BLOCKER B (missing P7 predecessor) is independent of Shared and admits no
deferral interpretation at all (Rule 7).

Why not write the new tests anyway: Rule 8 forbids committing code while BLOCKED,
and new iOS/macOS test files cannot be compiled or run here (no Shared) — shipping
unverifiable test code would risk latent compile errors presented as green
(Rule 1) and would not advance the gate. The correct action is to STOP, report
precisely, and let a JDK-equipped macOS runner (with P7 pages generated) execute
P9 to a real green.

Why not install a JDK / build Shared / generate P7 here: (a) apps/shared/** and
P7 are OUTSIDE this prompt's Allowed-Files (apps/apple/** + the log); (b) the KMP
Shared.xcframework is an explicit predecessor-tracked, CI-deferred artifact
(S3-0001) — working around it violates Rule 7 ("no predecessor bypass") and the
repo's own macOS-pending mechanism. Respecting the locked decision over a
local hack.

